If the solution to the convex problem is not rank-1, one common approach to approximate a rank-1 solution is to perform an eigenvalue decomposition on the PSD matrix. The eigenvector corresponding to the largest eigenvalue can then be used as an approximation to the rank-1 solution. This method ensures that the resulting solution closely approximates the original objective and constraints.

For example, consider the following convex optimization problem solved using CVX:

```matlab
