The term \( B \) involves the optimization variable \( t \), which makes the constraint non-convex. Specifically, the expression \( t \cdot \text{trace}(Ke \cdot W1) / (t-1) \) is non-convex because \( t \) is an optimization variable. CVX, which is designed for convex optimization, cannot handle this directly.

