   [value,num] = max(diag(D));
   x = sqrt(value)*V(:,num);
   X = reshape(x(1:Nt*L),Nt,L);
   ```

This approach uses binary variables to model the maximum element and ensures that the constraints are convex. The `abs(M(i,j)) <= z` constraint ensures that `z` is at least as large as any element in \( M \).

