To formulate the objective function in MATLAB using CVX, you can use the `rel_entr` function to handle the concave logarithmic term. Specifically, you can use the identity:

\[
\alpha_k \log_2(1 + \frac{y}{\alpha_k}) = -\text{rel\_entr}(\alpha_k, \alpha_k + y)
\]

where \( y = \frac{E_k |g_k|^2}{\sum_{l=1}^{K_{c}} P_l |g_{l,k}|^2 + \sigma_z^2} \).

