### Question 3: How to transform cell objects into numerical arrays to attach dual variables?

**Answer:**
To attach dual variables to constraints that are initially in cell array form, you can transform them into numerical arrays. For example:

```matlab
cvx_begin
    variable x(n) complex;     
    dual variable y;
    dual variable z;
    variable t;
    minimize (t);         
    L1 = complex_lorentz(m);   
    y: [A*x+b; c*x+d] == [L1.x; L1.y];
    L2 = complex_lorentz(n);       
    z: [x;t]  ==  [L2.x; L2.y];         
cvx_end
```

For a more robust solution, especially when dealing with complex variables, you can use real and imaginary parts separately:

```matlab
cvx_begin
    variable x(n) complex;     
    dual variable y;
    dual variable z;
    variable t;
    minimize (t);         
    L1 = lorentz(2*m);   
    y: [real(A*x+b); imag(A*x+b); real(c*x+d)] == [L1.x; L1.y];
    L2 = lorentz(2*n);       
    z: [real(x);imag(x);t]  ==  [L2.x; L2.y];         
cvx_end
```

