\[
\text{minimize} \quad -\text{trace}(A \cdot X)
\]
subject to:
\[
\text{trace}(A) = k
\]
\[
A \geq 0
\]
\[
A \leq I
\]

However, this problem is non-convex due to the constraints on \( A \). Additionally, if \( X \) is a CVX variable or expression, it will violate the DCP rules and cannot be solved using CVX. Ensure that \( X \) is a numeric matrix, not a CVX variable or expression.

