**Question:**
How to manage the constraint in CVX where either buying or selling power from/to the grid is allowed at a time?

**Answer:**
To enforce the constraint that at any time \( t \), either buying or selling power from/to the grid is allowed, but not both, you can use a Big M approach. Here is how you can modify your CVX program:

1. Introduce a binary variable \( b(t) \) to indicate whether buying power is active at time \( t \).
2. Add constraints to link \( b(t) \) with \( pg\_buy(t) \) and \( pg\_sell(t) \).

```matlab
cvx_begin
    variables p(T,d) pg_buy(T,1) pg_sell(T,1);
    variable b(T,1) binary;
    minimize(sum(alpha1*p(:,1).^2 + beta1*p(:,1) + alpha2*p(:,2).^2 + beta2*p(:,2) + alpha3*p(:,3).^2 + beta3*p(:,3) +...
    u'.*pg_buy - u'.*pg_sell));

    subject to
        sum(p,2) + pg_buy == D' + pg_sell;
        0 <= p(:,1) <= 4;
        0 <= p(:,2) <= 6;
