**Question:**
How can I use the infinity symbol (Inf) in constraints to express the condition "0 <= x(1) <= x(2) <= ... <= x(N)" in CVX?

**Answer:**
CVX does not support using infinity (Inf) in constraints directly. To express the condition "0 <= x(1) <= x(2) <= ... <= x(N)", you should avoid using Inf and instead use a series of explicit inequalities. For example, you can write:

```matlab
x(1) >= 0;
x(2) >= x(1);
x(3) >= x(2);
...
x(N) >= x(N-1);
```

This approach ensures that each element of the vector \( x \) is greater than or equal to the previous one, starting from 0. This method is compatible with CVX and avoids the need for using Inf in constraints.

