**Objective Function:**
\[
\mathop{\min}_{X,Y} P_{\text{tot}}(X) + \mu(\langle\bar{Y}\rangle - \lambda_{\max}(\bar{Y}))
\]

**Constraints:**
1. \(\bar{Y} := \left[\matrix{Y & \cal L(X) \\ \cal L^H(X) & 1}\right] \succeq 0\)
2. \(\sigma_s^2 \bf Y(i, i) \geq \alpha_i \left(\sigma_s^2 \sum_{j \neq i} \langle l_i l_i^H X h_j h_j^H X^H \rangle + \sigma_{\text{re}}^2 \langle l_i l_i^H X X^H \rangle + \sigma_{\text{de}}^2\right), \quad i=1,2,\ldots,M\)

**Function Definitions:**
- \(P_{\text{tot}}(X) = \langle (\sigma_s^2 H H^H + \sigma_{\text{re}}^2 I_N) X^H X \rangle\)
- \(\cal L(X) = (l_1^H X h_1, l_2^H X h_2, \ldots, l_M^H X h_M)^T\)

**Variables:**
- \(X\) is an \(N \times N\) matrix.
- \(Y\) is an \(M \times M\) matrix.
- \(H\) is an \(N \times M\) matrix.
- \(l_1, l_2, \ldots, l_M\) and \(h_1, h_2, \ldots, h_M\) are \(N \times N\) matrices.
- \(\sigma_s^2, \sigma_{\text{re}}^2, \sigma_{\text{de}}^2\) are constants.
- \(\alpha\) is a threshold.

